{
  "version": 1,
  "source": "Bonney Forge Branch Connections catalog",
  "standard": "MSS SP-97",
  "legend": {
    "A": "Height from the branch (outlet) end of the fitting to the crotch at the run pipe, inches. Installed height per catalog: L = A + (run pipe OD)/2 + root gap.",
    "B": "Width across the fitting at the branch end (upper body), per catalog diagram, inches.",
    "C": "Width across the fitting at the base/crotch where it meets the run pipe, per catalog diagram, inches.",
    "D": "Size-on-size tables only: opening (bore) diameter shown on the catalog end view, inches. For sockolet class 3000 size-on-size the catalog prints D as a decimal bore matching pipe ID.",
    "E": "Sockolet only: socket depth per catalog diagram, inches."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Printed fractional inches were converted to decimals exactly (e.g. 1 5/16 -> 1.3125).",
    "class 'XXS' is printed in the catalog as 'DBL. EXTRA STRONG & SCH. 160'.",
    "Rows with runFrom == runTo == branch are from the catalog's SIZE ON SIZE tables; other rows are from the REDUCING tables, whose single set of dimensions applies to all run sizes in runFrom-runTo (run ranges taken from the catalog's RUN SIZE CONSOLIDATIONS grids; a FLAT version covers runs larger than NPS 36, welding caps, elliptical heads and flat surfaces).",
    "runFrom/runTo omitted where the catalog prints no run range: weldolet STD/XS branches NPS 8 and larger and weldolet XXS branches NPS 5 and larger ('order to specific run size required'), and thredolet 6000 branches 1/4 and 3/8 (not in the class 6000 consolidation grid).",
    "Weights are pounds as printed; sockolet class 9000 weights are not published in the catalog.",
    "Weldolet STD reducing NPS 36 dimension C is printed 26 1/2 in the catalog (suspected misprint of 36 1/2); transcribed as printed.",
    "Thredolet 3000 reducing NPS 1 1/2 dimension B is printed 2 7/16 (sockolet/weldolet equivalents print 2 7/8); transcribed as printed."
  ],
